WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:06.260
We have a corona virus stimulus deal that
has finally been reached, and as some of you

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:11.559
might have heard on my livestreams, every
day there's like three proposals floated and

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:12.559
maybe it's going to happen.

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:13.559
Maybe it's not.

00:00:13.559 --> 00:00:15.789
And then it gets canceled or replaced with
something else.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:21.770
So because we all along, if I had talked about
every possible deal, the entire show would

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:23.380
have been just possible deals.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.000
That didn't become a reality.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.070
We just decided we're going to wait and then
we'll discuss the deal once it's actually

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.070
done.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:33.230
The priorities for me are we've got to bail
people out.

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:38.950
People with bills, people with expenses, people
who need money and may no longer have a job.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.500
We've got to do something about small business.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.820
Very, very important because a lot of small
businesses can't weather this.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:47.989
I'm talking to small business owners all the
time in my neighborhood and other neighborhoods

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:53.840
in Boston who say, you know, I can make 30
percent of what I was making before.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.480
But the problem is my rent is 40 percent.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:57.550
So I need something.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:00.300
I need some kind of bridge to get me there.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:04.809
And you want to provide capital strategically
to reduce interruptions of different kinds,

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:10.450
prevent the unemployment rate from exploding
as much as it would without some incentive

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:14.130
for small businesses to keep people on, etc..

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:17.360
This is the largest stimulus package in American
history.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:23.420
Now, a stimulus package, the concept of a
stimulus package is it's a Keynesian idea.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:29.630
The idea being government spending can lessen
the severity of a recession.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:30.630
Stimulate the economy.

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:31.630
Boost employment.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:32.630
Boost spending.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:33.630
That's the framework.

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:34.630
It's a Keynesian framework.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:39.300
We're talking about this deal was reached
just hours ago, around 1:30 a.m.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.250
Eastern Time, very early this morning.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:48.280
Here is Republican Senate Majority Leader
Mitch McConnell announcing it at last.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:50.549
We have a deal.

00:01:50.549 --> 00:01:56.270
After days of intense discussions, the Senate
has reached a bipartisan agreement on a Head

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:58.979
Start relief package for this pandemic.

00:01:58.979 --> 00:02:03.970
It will rush new resources onto the front
lines of our nation's health care fight, and

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:09.004
it will inject trillions of dollars of cash
into the economy as fast as possible.

00:02:09.004 --> 00:02:13.640
As you can tell there, Mitch McConnell just
overwhelmed with emotion over this historic

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:14.640
deal.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:15.640
So what's in it?

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:16.680
Some of the details are still being worked
out.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.150
Some of the language is still being written.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:19.470
As of as of this second.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:21.200
But here's what we have so far.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.340
It'll be a two trillion dollar stimulus package.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:29.340
People individuals earning up to $75000 in
income will get a 12 hundred dollar One-Time

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:30.440
check.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:33.060
Couples double the money for double the income
limit.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.060
Twenty four hundred dollars.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.400
If as a couple you earn up to 150000.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:42.290
You get an additional $500 per child based
on what we saw an hour ago.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:45.170
Again, some of the final details may change.

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:51.209
The twelve hundred dollar check starts to
phase out as you approach ninety nine thousand

00:02:51.209 --> 00:02:55.790
dollars in income as an individual or one
hundred ninety eight thousand as a couple.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:03:01.629
And once you get to that level ninety nine
K per person, you lose the 12, you lose all

00:03:01.629 --> 00:03:05.040
the money, you get zero after that point.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.160
Unemployment insurance will be expanded to
include people that are furloughed, gig workers,

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.160
freelancers.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:11.160
Right.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.870
People that would not normally qualify for
unemployment insurance.

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:15.690
They will also be adding.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:18.300
And this is one of the things that's a probably.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.580
But we don't know for sure yet.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:24.150
It looks like they're going to increase the
unemployment payments by six hundred bucks

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:28.099
a week for four months above the state base.

00:03:28.099 --> 00:03:31.269
Different states unemployment insurance is
state based.

00:03:31.269 --> 00:03:36.500
So the benefit in Massachusetts may be different
from the benefit in Florida or in California.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.750
That'll be upped by six hundred bucks a week
by the federal government.

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:45.920
There will be an employee retention tax credit
for businesses to keep people on.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:51.769
So we've seen two versions between 25 and
$50 billion for passenger airlines, between

00:03:51.769 --> 00:03:57.900
four and eight billion for cargo airlines,
17 billion for companies determined to be

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.870
important to national security.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:05.769
The details, of course, still remain to be
determined there, roughly $500 billion in

00:04:05.769 --> 00:04:07.580
a corporate liquidity program.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.770
These would be loans to businesses through
banks.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:14.660
Very important to understand that would be
through banks.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:20.629
And then another 367 billion, roughly through
a small business loan program, through the

00:04:20.629 --> 00:04:27.199
Small Businesses Association, 30 billion in
education funding, 25 billion in transit funding.

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:28.860
So this is the bulk of it.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:35.309
Now, there's a question about the income limit
on the twelve hundred dollar check 75k.

00:04:35.309 --> 00:04:37.569
What's the process and verification of that?

00:04:37.569 --> 00:04:43.199
If it's based on 2019 income, a lot of people
haven't filed their 20 19 tax returns.

00:04:43.199 --> 00:04:44.259
So what happens there?

00:04:44.259 --> 00:04:45.259
We don't know.

00:04:45.259 --> 00:04:50.490
There's the idea that you would use twenty
eighteen income if you've not yet filed your

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.500
2019 tax return.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:53.600
Excuse me.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.099
Could that be gamed in some way?

00:04:56.099 --> 00:04:57.539
We don't know.

00:04:57.539 --> 00:04:59.189
But this is part of the details.

00:04:59.189 --> 00:05:02.069
Well, that still needs to be worked out.

00:05:02.069 --> 00:05:05.949
Another question is how does this impact self-employed
people?

00:05:05.949 --> 00:05:10.409
There are some other specifics that need to
be sorted out, but it's finally happening.

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:12.659
It's happening far too late.

00:05:12.659 --> 00:05:17.610
It's happening after a lot of personal financial
damage has already happened to people who

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:21.180
have been laid off for one week, two weeks,
even longer in some cases.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:28.479
Chuck Schumer, Senate minority leader, says
that Trump's businesses will not be eligible

00:05:28.479 --> 00:05:30.449
for any of this stuff.

00:05:30.449 --> 00:05:32.449
That's an assertion from Chuck Schumer.

00:05:32.449 --> 00:05:36.960
I've not yet seen any language that makes
that clear.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:41.129
This is the framework we have so far in the
background of all this.

00:05:41.129 --> 00:05:46.330
Donald Trump increase increasingly wants to
reopen everything or close to everything on

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:48.810
Easter Sunday, April 12th.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:50.499
I want to talk about that next.

00:05:50.499 --> 00:06:37.240
And we'll be doing sort of deeper dove into
that a little bit later

00:06:37.240 --> 00:07:16.139
in 
the program.

